WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.757
Test the individual pieces before testing the whole agent.

00:00:03.757 --> 00:00:07.117
First, test retrieval with a known query.

00:00:07.117 --> 00:00:12.602
If the expected document is missing, the problem is retrieval or indexing.

00:00:12.602 --> 00:00:15.967
Test the grader with evidence you know should pass.

00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:20.232
If it fails, the problem is the grading rule or threshold.

00:00:20.232 --> 00:00:26.770
Test query rewriting. Make sure the rewritten query actually changes when correction is needed.

00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:30.156
Test generation with a fixed evidence set.

00:00:30.156 --> 00:00:32.826
Check whether the model stays grounded.

00:00:32.826 --> 00:00:37.831
Only after those components work should you test the full controller trajectory.

00:00:37.831 --> 00:00:40.426
This approach localizes failures.

00:00:40.939 --> 00:00:47.501
If the full agent fails but every component works independently, then the problem is likely orchestration:

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:52.155
wrong state updates, wrong route, or wrong stopping logic.
